From aefef4ebafd59e1d2d50c5d79752a787dd83da1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:18:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] S2-9: the workshop as kept panels on the GBA (part list,
 stat bars, header), flat backdrop

Where panels are kept (the GBA, and the native runner's panel model) the
workshop draws its part list's rows but the cursor's (the cursor's 12-row
pill is the panel's hole), the stat bars of both panes and the header strip
(tabs, title) as solid retained panels, shown last in the frame so the 2D
calls before them stay on the fast path. ui_window_open() leaves a panel's
rect out of a window, ui_style_use() sets the style a redrawn row reads,
ui_bar_still() and ui_backdrop_flat() are the two pixel-changing steps:
the stat bars lose their shine (it changed the panel every frame) and the
backdrop under the workshop is its bands without drifting dots, hearts and
twinkles (they were 2/3 of its 4 ms and show only in slivers around the
windows). The Dreamcast and the PS1 draw the screen as before.

test_panel: the workshop through the list, part values, the Armory and back
with the panel cache on and off, at both resolutions: every frame identical.
weld_slice.c joins the workshop overlay group on the PS1 (ovl_plan.py).

GBA (libmgba, speed2 action windows): workshop 17.9 -> 30.0 fps, part change
23.4 -> 30.0, armory 26.7 -> 30.0, no frame over 34 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
